  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to British Overseas NGO&apos;s for Development (Bond) and the UK Alliance</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through this grant, Bond and UK Alliance colleagues work with the FCDO to ensure that the UK has a strong, independent development sector that is delivering impact and learning together, along with being more data-driven and effective. The grant will help Bond and the UK Alliance to ensure that the sector, as well as the communities we support, can address the challenges we face in a coordinated way.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UK INGO coordination, collaboration with FCDO, as well as engagement with key international policy processes helps to contribute to more ambitious, effective and equitable responses to global development challenges. UK INGOs increasing their impact by collaborating and transforming to become more locally led, anti-racist organisations that respond effectively to LMIC priorities.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UK humanitarian and international development civil society organisations and their partners. Networks within the UK Alliance - Scotland&apos;s International Development Alliance, CADA Northern Ireland, South West International Development Network, Hub Cymru Africa, and the Small International Development Charities Network.</narrative>
  </description>
